97668d1b70d637abac76a16","html_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/commit/466449a4c69a07a1997668d1b70d637abac76a16"},{"sha":"9134f3a0d30ecaf4f5395b5a9bd9f4dfe4629ca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/commits/9134f3a0d30ecaf4f5395b5a9bd9f4dfe4629ca9","html_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/commit/9134f3a0d30ecaf4f5395b5a9bd9f4dfe4629ca9"}]}],"files":[{"sha":"5366d3b1caa42e04fa32447d89a72f4eea7a5bd9","filename":"AGENTS.md","status":"modified","additions":9,"deletions":4,"changes":13,"blob_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/blob/797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1/AGENTS.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/raw/797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1/AGENTS.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/contents/AGENTS.md?ref=797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1","patch":"@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ servers for builds, VM hosting and graphical acceptance.\n Connection pins, host selection, visual evidence and\n golden-image transfer rules are in `docs/lab/remote-builders.md`. On these five servers,\n the user authorizes dependency/tool setup and testing with passwordless\n-`sudo -n`; preserve existing projects and desktop work. Keep the SSH private key\n+`sudo -n`; preserve other sessions' projects and desktop work. Keep the SSH private key\n on the workstation.\n \n Aurora's Toolbx build, native session, Proton lab session, Atomic home and KWallet\n@@ -28,9 +28,14 @@ one, take its lock with `python3 tools/lab/desktop_lock.py acquire`, heartbeat i\n and release it only after its cleanup check passes. Never wait for another\n session's reply while holding a lock: notify the affected session and coordinator\n of the exact PIDs, intended action and a deadline at least 10 minutes ahead;\n-silence means go after that deadline. Before any logout or display-server restart,\n-check for Patrick's own apps. If any are present, ask Patrick first; his apps are\n-never leftovers, and silence never means go.\n+silence means go after that deadline. Nothing on these five machines is Patrick's:\n+applications in a desktop session, pending system updates and package state there\n+are lab state, and no logout, display-server restart, session switch or package\n+change on a builder needs his approval. Before one, check that no other session\n+holds work on that host. The lab's own package rules still apply: read every\n+`apt` or `dnf` transaction before confirming it, and never install, upgrade or\n+downgrade a compositor or desktop package, which would change the desktop under\n+test. His workstation is the one machine that is his.\n SSH builds and VMs on the builders are shared; heavy work stays off the workstation.\n The full rules, including one coordinator per session family, are in\n `docs/lab/remote-builders.md` under \"Sharing the lab between concurrent sessions\"."},{"sha":"d0e2af5ecb169a148e2caba8b84928d56738b828","filename":"docs/automation/agents.md","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":4,"changes":11,"blob_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/blob/797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1/docs%2Fautomation%2Fagents.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/raw/797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1/docs%2Fautomation%2Fagents.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/contents/docs%2Fautomation%2Fagents.md?ref=797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1","patch":"@@ -110,16 +110,19 @@ Prefer the [Fedora, Debian, Kubuntu, Mint and Aurora physical servers](../lab/re\n for builds, VMs and native graphical acceptance on their GNOME/Plasma/Cinnamon\n desktops; use local VMs only when the required remote host/profile\n is unavailable or unsuitable, and record why. Passwordless `sudo -n` setup is\n-authorized on all five servers. Preserve their existing projects and desktops;\n+authorized on all five servers. Preserve other sessions' projects and desktop work there;\n keep the workstation SSH key local. Check KVM, capacity and ports on the actual\n VM host before launch. A physical host's OS/desktop is not a substitute for a\n different version in the declared acceptance matrix. Take and heartbeat the desktop\n lock before GUI work; release it after verified cleanup. Never wait for another\n session's reply while holding a lock: notify the affected session and coordinator\n of the exact PIDs, intended action and a deadline at least 10 minutes ahead;\n-silence means go after that deadline. Before any logout or display-server restart,\n-check for Patrick's own apps. If any are present, ask Patrick first; his apps are\n-never leftovers, and silence never means go.\n+silence means go after that deadline. Nothing on a builder is Patrick's: applications in a desktop session, pending\n+system updates and package state there are lab state, and no logout, display-server\n+restart, session switch or package change on a builder needs his approval. Before\n+one, check that no other session holds work on that host. The lab's package rules\n+still apply: read every transaction first, and never change a compositor or desktop\n+package.\n The automatic nightly desktop check runs from a d69 timer across the five builders\n and reports to pinned issue #1003; release lab leases before 12:15 UTC. See\n [Sharing the lab between concurrent sessions](../lab/remote-builders.md#sharing-the-lab-between-concurrent-sessions)."},{"sha":"d51cc6add8132a5bb1c526a44cd072bb4e0a28eb","filename":"docs/lab/remote-builders.md","status":"modified","additions":12,"deletions":8,"changes":20,"blob_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/blob/797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1/docs%2Flab%2Fremote-builders.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/raw/797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1/docs%2Flab%2Fremote-builders.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/contents/docs%2Flab%2Fremote-builders.md?ref=797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1","patch":"@@ -279,8 +279,8 @@ desktop's screen-sharing consent once. On k72 the two servers share port 5900,\n one per session type, so the wall tile works in either login. Since 2026-10-20\n k72's default session is Plasma Wayland (`Session=plasma.desktop` in SDDM's\n autologin, `/etc/sddm.conf`). Switch it to `plasmax11.desktop` only when a check\n-needs KDE/X11, then switch it back. Each switch restarts `sddm` and logs\n-Patrick out, so the coordinator checks for his apps first.\n+needs KDE/X11, then switch it back. Each switch restarts `sddm` and ends the\n+desktop session, so check first that no other session holds work on k72.\n \n k72 has two outputs. HDMI-A-1 is forced on with the headless EDID\n (`drm.edid_firmware=HDMI-A-1:edid/patrick-headless.bin`). Since the 2026-10-20\n@@ -570,8 +570,8 @@ python3 tools/lab/desktop_lock.py break f44 --session ID --reason TEXT\n   coordinator, do other work and try again later. Between session families, the\n   lock goes to whoever takes it first.\n - `acquire` lists what's already on the host, such as an earlier holder's\n-  processes or Patrick's apps. Those aren't yours: leave them and tell your\n-  coordinator. `status` shows who released or broke the lock last.\n+  processes. Those aren't yours: leave them and tell your coordinator. `status`\n+  shows who released or broke the lock last.\n \n ### Release only after a full cleanup check\n \n@@ -617,10 +617,14 @@ the host, with the old lock and the cleanup check.\n - Processes left by a session that holds no lock on that host are leftovers, and\n   your logout may end them. Never pattern-kill. Kill only the exact PIDs you\n   started; other sessions' PIDs need the coordinator's OK.\n-- Patrick's own apps in a desktop session (browsers, terminals, btop, other\n-  agents such as Codex) are never leftovers. Before any logout or display-server\n-  restart, check the session for them. If any are there, ask Patrick, and here\n-  silence never means go.\n+- Nothing on a builder is Patrick's. Applications left open in a desktop session\n+  (browsers, terminals, btop), a pending system update and the installed package\n+  state are lab state. A logout, display-server restart, session switch or\n+  package change on a builder needs no approval from him; say in your report\n+  what you did. The check before one is for other sessions' work, as above, and\n+  the package rules below still hold (read every transaction; never change the\n+  desktop under test). His workstation is the one machine that is his, and it\n+  stays hands-off.\n - A relayed approval with a condition, such as \"Yes, coordinate first\", means\n   \"notify the affected sessions with a deadline\", not \"wait for their reply\".\n   If your own permission check blocks a relayed approval, ask Patrick in your"},{"sha":"1a333ec5e9f31eb80f859f805616ccdbc256ffef","filename":"docs/testing/acceptance-matrix.md","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":4,"changes":8,"blob_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/blob/797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1/docs%2Ftesting%2Facceptance-matrix.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/raw/797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1/docs%2Ftesting%2Facceptance-matrix.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/contents/docs%2Ftesting%2Facceptance-matrix.md?ref=797321956d759a0ad4bcb8cb22c9fc12a03b32d1","patch":"@@ -335,7 +335,7 @@ memory window and the coordinator's OK for each logout.\n   - **Updates** shows **Channel** on *Nightly*, the build's own (*Stable* and *Nightly* are the only choices since #344), with a status from the live app.put.gd feed.\n   - **Check now** works, and the nightly channel shows no notification.\n - **I. Start at login:** turn on **Launch at login**, then do a real logout and login. Put.gd must start from the AppImage.\n-  - Physical desktops: only with the coordinator's OK, and only after checking that none of Patrick's apps are open.\n+  - Physical desktops: with the coordinator's OK, after checking that no other session holds work on the host.\n   - VMs: through their autologin.\n - **J. Update check:** `appimageupdatetool --check-for-update` against the published zsync gives the correct answer for the feed at that moment. The full N→N+1 update is #296's check.\n - **K. Clean exit and cleanup:** quit from the tray, and nothing of put.gd keeps running.\n@@ -490,8 +490,8 @@ Each resident runs with private `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`,\n - **U11. Start at login after an update.** Turn on **Launch at login** on N. Update in-app without a\n   restart (and, on a second run, with appimageupdatetool). Then a real logout and login. Login starts\n   N+1 from the same folder.\n-  - Physical desktops: only with the coordinator's OK, after checking that none of Patrick's apps are\n-    open. VMs: through their autologin.\n+  - Physical desktops: with the coordinator's OK, after checking that no other session holds work on\n+    the host. VMs: through their autologin.\n - **U12. Refusals.** Each reason is shown in Settings and in `update.status`, and the image is unchanged:\n   - the AppImage's folder isn't writable;\n   - the file belongs to another user;\n@@ -643,7 +643,7 @@ On the accepted nightly, installed by item L.\n - **I. Start at login:** turn on **Launch at login** on the default profile.\n   - `~/.config/autostart/putgd.desktop` is written with `Exec=\"/usr/bin/putgd-launcher\" --background` and `X-putgd-Managed=true` (record its bytes).\n   - After a real logout and login, the resident runs from `/usr/bin/putgd`.\n-  - Physical desktops: only with the coordinator's OK, and only after checking that none of Patrick's apps are open. VMs: through their autologin.\n+  - Physical desktops: with the coordinator's OK, after checking that no other session holds work on the host. VMs: through their autologin.\n - **J. Package manager view:**\n   - `apt update` verifies the live `InRelease`, and `apt-cache policy putgd` shows the installed version as pkg.put.gd nightly's candidate. On Fedora, `dnf check-update putgd` verifies `repomd.xml` and lists nothing newer.\n   - Settings says *Up to date*."}]}